{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After a confirmed merge, status can persistently direct an agent to review or land the already merged PR."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A new PR head can invalidate an approval without appearing in the digest, causing the agent to miss required review work."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The digest can send an agent to review an unfinished head while requested changes are still running, wasting review work."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A historical blocker obscures a closed PR and directs the agent toward a landing request that will be refused."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable privacy policy allows mutations to succeed while hiding their receipts, making follow-up difficult and duplicate submissions possible."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable privacy policy causes status to succeed without the state or guidance the agent needs to continue."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Unicode formatting controls can make a quoted PR title visually misleading, although an escape from the quoted data boundary was not reproduced."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid approval with no saved snapshot is presented as requiring another review, potentially wasting review work."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The digest can direct review of a still-running PR even though the review API refuses it."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A nonexistent run produces an inaccurate HTTP error category while still returning an accurate error message."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"The documented Codex command uses Claude's consumer cursor and can omit work that Codex has not handled."},{"id":"C13","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A malformed successful backend response is presented as a successful review or land receipt, potentially misleading the agent about the mutation."}]}